{
    "UniqueID": "hw_dancingplague",
    "//DancingPlague": "Feature 28, the dancing plague (plan section 28, pack Prompt 41): the fourth Harsh Wilds AFFLICTION, on the spirit sickness file's chassis (Documentation/Design/Harsh_Wilds_As_Built.md 7.1) with ONE deliberate difference, which the plan's row asks for ('stamina drain and hunger statuses for a few hours'): it FALLS BY ITSELF. BaseRatePerTick -1, so a roll of HW_DANCE_PER_ROLL = 16 lasts 16 ticks (four hours) and the cap of 32 is eight hours; the Afflictions gate marks the row Decays and still demands every other chassis rule. Its SOURCE is a rolled STA, Tgr_HW_DancingPlague, armed by the hw_ring_dance marker that 'Dance in the Ring' (CardData/Location/hw_fairy_ring, night only, an hour) writes: Nothing (weight HW_DANCE_NOTHING = 1) against Plague (weight 1) writes +16. CURE: the Cleansing Smudge's second action, which clears the whole stat (-32) at a lit fire; Tgr_HW_DancingSwitchOff clears it while [Threats] DancingPlague is off. COST, statuses only, both RATES on the vanilla Stamina (1cfd30cf13b69b949a0ac521f55a59a2, base +2 a tick, so -3 nets -1 and -4 nets -2) and Energy (9e03b1c645e4c1c40b382ceac8387d4e, the food-energy stat, -0.5 then -1 a tick) - the plan's 'stamina drain and hunger'. Neither stat is watched by a trigger this affliction can land on, and the affliction touches no Stress, so [clamp-rate] has nothing to pin. Every number is a TUNABLE PLACEHOLDER, session-inferred and unmeasured against play.",
